  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> be differentiable at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>c</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math>, then at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>g</mi></math>&nbsp;is:"
  },
